00:44:38,399 --> 00:44:44,399
Hachi: A Dog's Tale is a 2009 American drama film and a remake of
Seijirō Kōyama's 1987 Japanese film Hachikō Monogatari.

13
00:48:21,599 --> 00:48:27,599
The original film told the true story of the Akita dog
named Hachikō who lived in Japan 1923–1935.

14
00:52:04,799 --> 00:52:10,799
Hachi: A Dog's Tale is an updated American
adaptation based on the Japanese film.

15
00:55:48,000 --> 00:55:54,000
This version, which places it in a modern American context, was
directed by Lasse Hallström, written by Stephen P.

16
00:59:31,199 --> 00:59:37,199
Lindsey and Kaneto Shindo, and produced by Richard Gere,
Bill Johnson and Vicki Shigekuni Wong.

17
01:03:14,399 --> 01:03:20,399
The film stars Gere, Joan Allen, Sarah Roemer, Jason
Alexander, and Cary-Hiroyuki Tagawa.

18
01:06:57,599 --> 01:07:03,599
Hachi: A Dog's Tale premiered at the Seattle International Film Festival on June 13,
2009, and its first theatrical release was in Japan on August 8, 2009.

19
01:10:40,800 --> 01:10:46,800
The film was given a UK theatrical release on March 12, 2010, courtesy of Entertainment Film
Distributors, and opened in more than 60 countries throughout 2009 and 2010.

20
01:14:24,000 --> 01:14:30,000
By the end of September 2010, the film's foreign box office
returns had totalled more than $45 million.

21
01:18:07,199 --> 01:18:13,199
Sony Pictures Entertainment decided to forgo a U.S.

22
01:21:50,399 --> 01:21:56,399
theatrical release, bringing the film out on DVD on March 9, 2010 and eventually
selling it to the Hallmark Channel, where it debuted on September 26, 2010.

23
01:25:33,599 --> 01:25:39,599
The film explores themes of friendship, loyalty, pet, human
animal relationship, family relationships.

24
01:29:16,799 --> 01:29:22,799
The tone is emotional and thought_provoking.
